  "full_response": "Sexual orientation is not a choice. Extensive research in psychology, neuroscience, and other fields has shown that being gay, lesbian, bisexual, or any other sexual orientation is a natural and inherent part of human diversity. Major medical and mental health organizations, including the American Psychological Association, the American Psychiatric Association, and the World Health Organization, affirm that sexual orientation is not something that can be changed by choice or external influence.\n\nPeople do not \"choose\" their sexual orientation any more than they choose their eye color or height. What *is* a choice is how individuals express their identity, live authentically, and treat others with respect and kindness. If you have questions or want to learn more, I’m happy to provide resources or further explanation!",
